# umbra default egress allowlist (shipped; don't edit -- add your own entries
# to ~/.config/umbra/egress/allow, or click "Always allow" on a prompt).
#
# An entry covers the domain and all its subdomains on ports 80/443.
# "host:port" entries cover exactly that port. Lines starting with # are
# comments. Kept deliberately narrow: every entry here is a place an agent
# could send data without asking you, so general-purpose upload/paste/doc
# services are NOT on it (they prompt).

# --- Claude Code
anthropic.com
claude.ai
claude.com

# --- Antigravity (agy) / Google model APIs, sign-in, feature flags, avatars
googleapis.com
antigravity.google
antigravity-unleash.goog
accounts.google.com
lh3.googleusercontent.com
# agy browser automation downloads Playwright's Chromium builds (exact hosts;
# never azureedge.net as a whole -- anyone can serve content from it)
playwright.azureedge.net
playwright-akamai.azureedge.net
playwright-verizon.azureedge.net
cdn.playwright.dev

# --- OpenCode
opencode.ai
models.dev

# --- source hosting (read-mostly; pushing still needs credentials you didn't pass)
github.com
githubusercontent.com
gitlab.com

# --- package registries
registry.npmjs.org
registry.yarnpkg.com
jsr.io
pypi.org
files.pythonhosted.org
crates.io
static.rust-lang.org
proxy.golang.org
sum.golang.org
bun.sh
